      "vision_reason": "A carved wooden prestige staff with spherical finial and chain-link/spiral shaft decoration, a form used by Nguni pastoralist men (Zulu or Tsonga) in southern Africa; the museum itself attributes it to a Tsonga- or Zulu-style maker, so it plausibly belongs to the claimed group. Material is wood, not metal, so the category is misassigned.",
